# Audit run outputs — regenerable, and ~1.8 MB per run. The probes (audit/*.py)
# and the audit scripts themselves are the durable part; these are just their output.
#
# Patterns are relative to THIS directory (a .gitignore applies below its own
# root), so the prefix is `audit/`, not `tmp/audit/` — the earlier `tmp/audit/`
# form matched nothing and every audit output was one `git add` from the repo.
audit/*.json
audit/*.log
audit/*.out
audit/*.err
audit/*.txt
